8
00:00:23,955 --> 00:00:26,760
First of all, what is machine learning?

9
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:32,070
A machine learning algorithm is a type of artificial intelligence or AI,

10
00:00:32,070 --> 00:00:36,285
where a computer is learning how to extract information from data.

11
00:00:36,285 --> 00:00:38,589
To train a machine learning algorithm,

12
00:00:38,589 --> 00:00:41,330
we have to fit it with example data.

13
00:00:41,330 --> 00:00:45,200
In this course, we'll be using a few different data-set.

14
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:47,510
But for now, we will focus on

15
00:00:47,510 --> 00:00:53,650
the German traffic sign recognition benchmark or GTSRB data-set.

16
00:00:53,650 --> 00:00:56,615
This data-set consists of thousands of

17
00:00:56,615 --> 00:01:00,320
images of traffic sign with their associated labels.

18
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:03,215
We will focus on classifying these traffic signs

19
00:01:03,215 --> 00:01:06,515
using different algorithm in the following lessons.

20
00:01:06,515 --> 00:01:10,610
In this lesson, we'll use it as an example of a task you could

21
00:01:10,610 --> 00:01:15,750
face in your future job as a machine learning engineer. Let's get started.

